practice_time = 60
practice_seeds = 1101, 1102, 1103, 1104, 1105, 1106, 1107, 1108, 1109, 1110, 1111, 1112, 1113, 1114, 1115, 1116, 1117, 1118, 1119, 1120
practice_instructions = You will play Tetris. Pieces fall from the top of the board one at a time. Fill a row completely and it clears. The game ends when the pile reaches the top of the board; when that happens, a new game starts and you keep playing.
practice_instructions_2 = Your goal is to score as many points as you can. Points come from clearing rows. Clearing several rows at once is worth much more than clearing them one at a time: four rows at once scores thirty times as much as one row. The box on the left shows your score, lines cleared, and level. The game speeds up as you clear more lines.
practice_instructions_3 = Move the piece left and right with the direction pad. Rotate it with the A and B buttons. Hold down on the direction pad to make it fall faster. When a game ends, press Start to begin the next one.
practice_instructions_4 = You will play for 45 minutes in four parts. First, one minute to get used to the controls. Then six minutes of play. Then 28 minutes of play. Then a final ten-minute part. In the final part the screen will show the standard game only. Your bonus is based on your score in that final part, so play to be as good as you can be by the end. Press Start when you are ready to try the controls.

